abstract: 'ML-independent structural tools for Herculaneum scroll surfaces:
  a topological grid metric that measures the scribe''s writing lattice without
  reading text, a void-aware layer-count reconciliation, and a synthetic scroll
  twin that sizes itself from the length of the work, crushes to the measured
  deformation, and supplies per-letter ground truth for testing the toolchain.
  Every mode ships with the pre-registered acceptance test that gates it.'
